    {
      "id": 19,
      "type": "Note",
      "title": "READ ME FIRST",
      "pos": [
        1700,
        0
      ],
      "size": [
        580,
        860
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 18,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "text": ""
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "SAGEATTENTION COMES FROM THE LAUNCH FLAG, NOT FROM A NODE.\n\nStart ComfyUI with --use-sage-attention. ComfyUI then hands SageAttention to\nSolAttnH3 as the backend it falls back to, and as the backend that recomputes\nthe sink's query rows. Without the flag you get PyTorch SDPA, roughly 2.5x\nslower at these shapes.\n\nDO NOT ADD 'Patch Sage Attention KJ' TO THIS GRAPH. It writes the same\ntransformer_options['optimized_attention_override'] key SolAttnH3 uses. They\noverwrite each other, last node in the chain wins, and the loser goes silent\n-- no warning, no log line, just the speed gone.\n\nREFERENCE IMAGES. Up to 9 sockets, ref_image_0 upward. Connect them in the\norder your <Picture N> tags use: <Picture 1> is ref_image_0. Three or four\nvaried shots hold identity far better than one. Unused sockets stay empty.\n\nref_image_size='match' scales each reference to the generation's pixel area.\n'max' uses the reference pipeline's 2048px short edge for best identity, and\nis several times slower -- reference tokens ride through EVERY sampling step,\nnot just the first.\n\nLENGTH snaps up to the model's 17k+5 grid: 124 (~5s), 141, 158, ..., 362\n(~15s). Off-grid values are rounded up silently, so 125 gives you 141.\n\nWHETHER SolAttnH3 PAYS DEPENDS ON LENGTH -- and this graph ships at 124,\nwhich is the length where it did NOT pay on the i2v sibling. Measured there\non an RTX 5080, NVFP4, 8 steps, real first frame:\n\n  124 frames   off  35.2s   on  39.0s   ->  0.90x, the node COSTS you 10%\n  362 frames   off 150.2s   on 137.1s   ->  1.10x, the node is worth it\n\nThe sink is recomputed densely on every sparse call, so a short sequence\ncannot earn it back. Reference images make the sink LARGER still, so ref2va\nshould need the longer length even more -- but that is reasoning from the\ni2v measurement, NOT a ref2va measurement. Nobody has timed this graph.\n\nSo: raise length toward 362 for real renders, and while you iterate at 124\neither set enabled=false or measure it yourself first. 124 is the default\nhere only because it is the safe one for VRAM -- 362 plus reference tokens\non a 16 GB card is untested and may not fit.\n\nCHECK IT IS RUNNING. Once per run the console prints:\n  [sol-attn-h3] SM120, CuTe DSL available, backend=cute_sm120, DiT blocks: 50\n  [sol-attn-h3] correctness gate PASS ...\n  [sol-attn-h3] routing density {...}\nbackend=triton on an SM89+ card means the CuTe runtime is missing.\nsparse_calls: 0 means every call declined; the reason is in 'declined'."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
